  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line. The demo prints `1` (only the Gadget is left) instead of `2`, and all 6 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:33`, `Cart.remove` filtered lines by the item's name (`l.item.name != sku`) instead of its SKU. The name `'Widget'` never equals `'sku-1'`, so nothing was ever removed.\n\n**Fix:** I changed the check to `l.item.sku != sku`, which matches how `Cart.add` identifies lines.\n\n**Tests:** pytest isn't installed here, so I ran them with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`. None of the existing tests call `Cart.remove`, so they would have passed with the bug too. The demo is what confirms the fix. I can add a regression test for `remove` if you want one.",
